        "claude_code_version": "2.1.281",
        "final_text": "Looking at the code structure, I can trace the issue:\n\n1. **requests/sessions.py** (line 115 in `resolve_redirects`): passes `params=req.params` to the redirect request\n2. **requests/models.py** (line 303-308 in `prepare_url`): appends params to the URL, even if the URL already has a query string\n\nWhen a redirect happens:\n- The location header contains a complete URL (potentially with query params already)\n- Line 115 in sessions.py then passes `params=req.params` again\n- The `prepare_url` method concatenates the existing query string with the new params, doubling them\n\nThe fix requires changing where redirect requests are made to not re-apply the original request's params, since the Location header from the server is already a complete URL.\n\n```json\n{\"files\":[\"requests/sessions.py\",\"requests/models.py\"]}\n```",
